  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Pampelonne is 4.5 km of fine sand over a 27-hectare area that made Saint-Tropez legendary: about twenty beach establishments and water activities welcome visitors in season (Club 55, Tahiti Plage and L'Épi Plage built its reputation, according to the Ramatuelle tourist office). It is the most famous beach in Ramatuelle.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Ramatuelle tourist office states (FAQ and 2025 "Dog friendly" leaflet) that all the town's beaches — Pampelonne bay, the Bonne Terrasse cove, L'Escalet beach and the Canadel coves — are open to dogs kept on a leash; swimming is allowed except in the ZRUB (zones reserved solely for bathing). No time slot is announced.</p>
      <p>The Pampelonne beach police regulation (2021, article 16) specifies: dogs may only walk on the beach on a leash; from 1 April to 15 October they are banned, even on a leash, in the zones reserved solely for bathers, but tolerated on a leash in the zones closed to motorised craft. Letting a dog foul the beach is forbidden (pick up after it). Category 2 dogs must be muzzled and held on a leash by an adult. These bathing zones are marked by the lifeguard posts (Gros Vallat, Patch, Tamaris), supervised in season only: ask them.</p>
      <p>Other useful points: the beach is reached by several entrances (route de Bonne Terrasse, chemin de Garonne, boulevard Patch, chemin des Tamaris, chemin des Moulins, route de Tahiti); in 2026, a free shuttle runs from the village from 15 June to 22 September, and Zou line 875 from 1 May to 27 September (Zou rules only admit harmless animals under 10 kg on a leash or in a carrier, per the tourist office leaflet). On the coastal path, dogs on a leash are tolerated, as long as they stay on the path.</p>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go:</strong> the regulation currently in force (the text we read dates from 2021; the commune's recent orders concern noise and pollution), the location of the bathers-only zones, and each beach establishment's own rules.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: on a 4.5 km beach, move away from the immediate surroundings of the beach establishments, often crowded, to leave room for your dog and others.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The coastal path leads to the Bonne Terrasse cove at the south of the bay, then to L'Escalet beach and Cap Taillat. The hilltop village of Ramatuelle rounds off the outing.</p>
      <p><small>Sources read on 07/11/2026: Ramatuelle tourist office (FAQ, 2025 Dog friendly leaflet), Pampelonne beach police regulation (2021) published by the commune, "Beach regulations" page on ramatuelle.fr.</small></p>
